---
description: Version history via jj — allowed operations and test rules
globs: iterthink/persistence/vcs.py,tests/v2/persistence/test_vcs*.py
alwaysApply: false
---

2.0 stores versions in `.iterthink/versions/` via `persistence/snapshots.py`
(slice A3). Do not add `persistence/vcs.py`. The notes below apply only if a
later version adopts jj (`docs/spec/README.md`, "Later").

- Call jj via subprocess with `--no-pager`, `--color never`, `-T` templates,
  list args, timeout. Parse template output, never human output.
- Repo is non-colocated: `.jj/` at the project root, no `.git`.
- Config is written by iterthink into the repo config, never a `.gitignore`.
- Allowed: snapshot, describe, new, workspace add/forget, bookmark create,
  restore --from, rebase of proposals, log, diff, op log.
- Forbidden on recorded history: `op undo`, `abandon`, `squash`, `util gc`,
  force push. Only a function named `erase_*` may use `abandon`/`gc`, and
  only with an audit event.
- Every public function returns typed results (change id, commit id), not raw text.
- Tests run against a real jj in `tmp_path` (`jj_bin` fixture). Do not mock jj
  in integration tests; unit tests may fake the subprocess layer.
